  /// value is omitted ( n: ), then the highest possible node index is used to
  /// end the range. Your accumulative node ranges must account for all nodes
  /// ( 0:n ). You can nest node ranges (for example, 0:10 and 4:5 ). In this
  /// case, the 4:5 range properties override the 0:10 properties.
  pub target_nodes: Str? = None
  /// The container details for the node range.
  pub container: ContainerProperties? = None
  /// The instance types of the underlying host infrastructure of a multi-node
  /// parallel job. This parameter isn't applicable to jobs that are running
  /// on Fargate resources. In addition, this list object is currently limited
  /// to one element.
  pub instance_types: List[Str]? = None
  /// This is an object that represents the properties of the node range for a
  /// multi-node parallel job.
  pub ecs_properties: EcsProperties? = None
  /// This is an object that represents the properties of the node range for a
  /// multi-node parallel job.
  pub eks_properties: EksProperties? = None
  /// Contains a list of consumable resources required by a job.
  pub consumable_resource_properties: ConsumableResourceProperties? = None
}

pub enum OrchestrationType: Str {
  Ecs = "ECS"
  Eks = "EKS"
  Unknown(value: Str)
}

pub enum PlatformCapability: Str {
  Ec2 = "EC2"
  Fargate = "FARGATE"
  ManagedInstances = "MANAGED_INSTANCES"
  Unknown(value: Str)
}

/// The configured capacity usage for a job queue snapshot, including the
